WEBVTT

00:02.710 --> 00:05.810
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy</b>

00:06.530 --> 00:11.830
<i>What is valued most highly at the 
prestigious Rigarden Magical Academy?</i>

00:15.530 --> 00:18.670
<i>Naturally, it's a talent for magic.</i>

00:19.940 --> 00:22.330
<i>So what of those with no aptitude for it?</i>

00:22.680 --> 00:25.940
<i>Is there any way for the talentless 
to advance at this academy?</i>

00:27.840 --> 00:30.340
<b>Dungeon, Floor 7</b>

00:34.540 --> 00:36.550
<i>To answer that question...</i>

00:40.730 --> 00:44.310
<i>I come to the dungeon to slay monsters!</i>

00:59.010 --> 00:59.950
<i>Even I...</i>

01:01.080 --> 01:02.950
<i>Even I can do it if I try!</i>

01:03.940 --> 01:05.990
<i>Even if I can't use magic!</i>

01:06.960 --> 01:11.960
Episode 1
Like a Lone Sword

01:13.670 --> 01:17.970
<b>Urbus Rigarden
The Capital of Magic</b>

01:17.970 --> 01:20.970
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy</b>

01:21.490 --> 01:26.230
Channeling a minute amount of magic 
into the balca ore and agni dust

01:26.230 --> 01:28.280
creates a lump of sulfur.

01:28.280 --> 01:31.480
Subsequently, it is possible 
to catalyze a brilliant flame.

01:32.210 --> 01:33.550
Correct.

01:33.110 --> 01:37.490
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy Professor
Edward Serfence</b>

01:33.550 --> 01:35.360
Now, let's see...

01:35.800 --> 01:37.490
I'll have <i>you</i> come up front.

01:38.350 --> 01:39.190
Will.

01:39.490 --> 01:42.240
<b>Familiar
Kiki</b>

01:40.110 --> 01:41.580
Will Serfort.

01:42.590 --> 01:43.870
Will Serfort!

01:45.500 --> 01:49.630
Y-Yes, sir! What is it, Professor Edward?

01:46.460 --> 01:49.630
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy Student, Sixth Year
Will Serfort</b>

01:49.880 --> 01:52.290
I told you to come down
to the front of the class.

01:53.300 --> 01:54.910
<i>This again?</i>

01:55.470 --> 01:56.760
Of course.

02:03.570 --> 02:06.270
What's wrong? It's a simple practical exercise.

02:06.740 --> 02:10.880
As you know, you need only use 
the catalyst to conjure the flame.

02:13.530 --> 02:14.830
O flames...

02:16.300 --> 02:17.900
spring forth!

02:32.210 --> 02:33.670
<i>Will...</i>

02:34.870 --> 02:36.170
Silence.

02:38.960 --> 02:43.930
To think a student at our institution is
 unable to use even the most basic of magics...

02:44.370 --> 02:46.380
As expected of a book learner.

02:46.380 --> 02:49.940
No wonder they say you're only an
honor student when it comes to note-taking.

02:50.620 --> 02:53.190
You are entirely beyond help.

02:54.590 --> 02:56.110
O flames...

02:56.110 --> 02:57.360
obey me.

03:07.450 --> 03:10.120
Refrain from demonstrations
without permission,

03:10.120 --> 03:11.840
Sion Ulster.

03:10.960 --> 03:17.170
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy Student, Sixth Year
Sion Ulster</b>

03:12.260 --> 03:15.440
I'm sorry, Professor Edward.

03:15.440 --> 03:18.380
It seems like Will isn't in top form,

03:18.720 --> 03:21.380
so I thought I'd help in his place.

03:22.890 --> 03:24.640
Well, as it happens, this will do.

03:24.900 --> 03:27.260
As all of you just saw...

03:29.890 --> 03:32.900
in this world, the supremacy
 of magic is absolute.

03:33.430 --> 03:35.270
Magic is authority.

03:35.540 --> 03:37.400
Strength of magic is power.

03:37.400 --> 03:39.400
Our heroes are mages!

03:40.010 --> 03:44.090
And here at this academy, 
your talent for magic is how you earn esteem.

03:44.930 --> 03:49.000
A no-talent who has theoretical knowledge,
but cannot perform even one bit of magic,

03:49.000 --> 03:52.100
is unfit to stand in these halls
that give rise to sages.

03:52.970 --> 03:56.000
Fools who dream above their stations

03:56.000 --> 03:59.680
should withdraw from 
this academy immediately.

04:09.830 --> 04:13.270
Flaunted your ineptitude 
yet again today, didn't you, laggard?

04:13.270 --> 04:14.900
Sion...

04:13.270 --> 04:17.020
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy Student, Sixth Year
Lyril Marze</b>

04:13.270 --> 04:17.070
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy Student, Sixth Year
Gordon Baret</b>

04:14.900 --> 04:17.520
I hear you went into the dungeon again, too.

04:18.020 --> 04:20.280
Taking out small fry
to scrape up some credits...

04:20.690 --> 04:22.070
Aren't you embarrassed?

04:23.780 --> 04:25.780
That's enough out of you boys!

04:25.780 --> 04:27.450
Well, well, Colette.

04:27.450 --> 04:33.160
For a <i>real</i> honor student like you to defend 
a failure like him, I just can't understand—

04:33.160 --> 04:36.210
Will is far kinder than you and
 works harder than anyone!

04:36.210 --> 04:38.670
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy Student, Sixth Year
Colette Loire</b>

04:36.480 --> 04:38.670
I won't have you insulting my friend!

04:40.580 --> 04:42.050
<i>Colette...</i>

04:47.130 --> 04:51.310
Kindness and hard work alone 
won't make a great mage out of anyone.

04:51.840 --> 04:53.180
Not to mention...

04:53.550 --> 04:56.920
becoming a Magia Vander is simply
a dream beyond dreams.

04:57.720 --> 05:02.690
Now then, spending any longer with
 this no-talent would be a waste of time.

05:02.690 --> 05:07.690
Like Professor Edward said, you should 
hurry up and leave this school already.

05:12.690 --> 05:14.460
Don't let them get to you.

05:14.760 --> 05:17.080
There's something wrong 
with Professor Edward too,

05:17.080 --> 05:19.630
making a laughingstock of you like that!

05:19.630 --> 05:21.160
It's all right, Colette.

05:21.460 --> 05:24.590
After all, it's true that I can't use magic.

05:25.270 --> 05:26.840
Will...

05:28.060 --> 05:32.290
Besides, if I've got a cute girl 
like you worried about me over it,

05:32.290 --> 05:33.850
then I count myself lucky.

05:37.200 --> 05:38.900
Wh-Where did that come from?!

05:38.900 --> 05:39.510
What?

05:38.900 --> 05:41.820
You say things like that now and again
with that meek expression!

05:41.820 --> 05:43.410
What are you after?

05:43.410 --> 05:45.900
Flattery will get you nowhere, you hear me?

05:45.900 --> 05:49.870
Wait, you don't use lines like that
on anyone and everyone, do you?!

05:49.870 --> 05:51.540
I-I'm sorry.

05:51.540 --> 05:54.870
Ever since I was little, 
I was taught to compliment girls.

05:55.130 --> 05:58.090
But even objectively speaking, 
you are cute, Colette.

05:57.540 --> 06:01.420
<b>CUTE CUTE CUTE CUTE CUTE CUTE CUTE CUTE</b>

05:58.090 --> 05:59.840
So I was just speaking the truth.

05:59.840 --> 06:00.810
I didn't mean anything—

06:00.810 --> 06:02.340
Enough!

06:02.340 --> 06:04.930
You don't have to say any more!

06:04.930 --> 06:06.480
A-All right.

06:09.570 --> 06:11.280
<i>I lost it for a moment there.</i>

06:11.280 --> 06:13.050
<i>I'm Colette Loire,</i>

06:13.050 --> 06:15.340
<i>the daughter of a noble family, 
if in name only.</i>

06:15.340 --> 06:16.920
<i>I must maintain my composure.</i>

06:19.370 --> 06:21.030
Is something wrong, Will?

06:23.140 --> 06:23.930
No.

06:25.000 --> 06:25.950
I was just...

06:26.860 --> 06:28.920
thinking how beautiful it is again today.

06:31.680 --> 06:33.540
It really is.

06:35.050 --> 06:37.130
It's such a warm light.

06:37.130 --> 06:43.220
The most powerful wizards, 
the Magia Vander, continue to uphold the sky.

06:50.500 --> 06:54.670
<i>Long ago, people knew nothing of the sky.</i>

06:55.180 --> 06:57.070
<i>They were trapped in darkness.</i>

06:57.880 --> 07:02.110
<i>The world was terrorized by the Celestial Host</i>

07:03.260 --> 07:07.040
<i>until five wizards rose up against them.</i>

07:12.340 --> 07:15.890
<i>These wizards turned back the invaders.</i>

07:15.890 --> 07:18.000
<i>They cast a seal over the sky...</i>

07:18.450 --> 07:20.680
<i>and brought peace to our world.</i>

07:26.150 --> 07:27.750
<i>The Magia Vander...</i>

07:28.430 --> 07:32.200
<i>That title that has been passed down 
ever since, given only to the strongest.</i>

07:32.990 --> 07:37.280
<i>Everyone dreams of it at least once—
the honor of becoming a mage.</i>

07:39.770 --> 07:45.930
Do you think that the Icemaiden's Wand, 
Albis Vina, is watching over us today, too?

07:46.270 --> 07:47.400
She is.

07:47.400 --> 07:48.160
What?

07:52.380 --> 07:54.160
<i>She's sitting by a window up top...</i>

07:56.420 --> 07:58.160
<i>looking this way.</i>

08:00.470 --> 08:02.060
The sun and moon?

08:03.580 --> 08:04.680
That's right!

08:04.680 --> 08:08.920
They say that the sun and moon are
 floating up there in the real sky.

08:08.920 --> 08:11.420
Is that true, Elfaria?

08:11.420 --> 08:15.930
And what's more, on the other side of the sky,
there's a beautiful sunset!

08:16.650 --> 08:19.410
It turns all kinds of things bright red.

08:19.410 --> 08:21.930
I hear it's the loveliest thing in the world!

08:23.330 --> 08:26.690
If we get as close as we can to the sky,
at the top of the tower...

08:27.240 --> 08:31.720
If we become Magia Vander,
maybe we can see the sunset.

08:33.720 --> 08:36.320
Then let's go and see it together!

08:40.280 --> 08:42.150
Yeah! It's a promise!

08:44.430 --> 08:48.250
<i>It was nothing more than an
 innocent childhood promise.</i>

08:49.560 --> 08:52.670
<i>But </i>she<i> was the real thing.</i>

08:53.560 --> 08:57.860
<i>With her talent, she became the youngest 
ever to earn the Magia Vander title,</i>

08:57.860 --> 08:59.740
<i>and left for the top of the tower.</i>

09:01.240 --> 09:02.520
<i>As for me...</i>

09:03.480 --> 09:05.980
<i>Being talentless, I'm even less than mediocre.</i>

09:06.820 --> 09:09.820
<i>But, unable to give up on 
the promise we made that day,</i>

09:10.360 --> 09:15.420
<i>I'm still scrambling, even now, 
to achieve my dream of standing beside her.</i>

09:16.380 --> 09:17.860
You...

09:17.860 --> 09:19.120
idiot!

09:21.370 --> 09:24.370
P-Professor Workner, please calm down!

09:24.370 --> 09:26.930
You hit the dungeon
without permission again, didn't you?

09:25.580 --> 09:31.260
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy Professor
Workner Norgram</b>

09:26.930 --> 09:29.210
And you went to the seventh floor solo?

09:29.210 --> 09:31.630
You really are going to get
 yourself killed one day!

09:32.380 --> 09:36.130
I-I'm sorry, Professor Workner!

09:38.920 --> 09:41.300
But, um...

09:41.300 --> 09:43.020
about my credits...

09:43.020 --> 09:45.180
Glare!

09:48.670 --> 09:51.070
That's one Evil Guard kill confirmed.

09:51.620 --> 09:54.280
You are hereby awarded two credits.

09:54.970 --> 09:56.030
All right!

10:07.130 --> 10:10.170
So you still haven't given up 
on becoming a Magia Vander?

10:11.950 --> 10:14.020
Is that... wrong of me?

10:18.690 --> 10:24.910
Listen, before you head up the tower,
you need to advance to the Upper Institute.

10:24.910 --> 10:27.220
And to do that, you'll need writing,

10:27.220 --> 10:27.810
spellwork,

10:28.170 --> 10:29.210
and praxis.

10:29.660 --> 10:32.430
You need a tremendous amount
of credits from the three curricula.

10:32.430 --> 10:36.970
And since you can't use magic, 
you'll never be able to earn spellwork credits.

10:37.320 --> 10:38.300
I know, sir!

10:38.300 --> 10:41.490
That's why I'm focusing on praxis, 
collecting credits in the dung—

10:41.490 --> 10:44.080
Will, I've told you this countless times,

10:44.540 --> 10:48.960
but advancing through praxis alone 
is effectively impossible.

10:51.310 --> 10:54.090
Especially for someone who can't use magic.

10:55.990 --> 10:59.220
Even so, I...

11:06.250 --> 11:07.720
In <i>any</i> event...

11:08.010 --> 11:11.230
stop thinking about becoming a 
Magia Vander when you may not even graduate!

11:11.570 --> 11:15.260
I already know that you failed to earn
any credits on your most recent exams.

11:15.260 --> 11:18.610
That means you need to earn 
four credits by the end of the week!

11:18.610 --> 11:20.740
What? B-By the end of <i>this</i> week?!

11:20.740 --> 11:22.990
But there are only two days left!

11:24.010 --> 11:25.860
Now that it's come to this...

11:25.860 --> 11:27.540
I will devote everything I have...

11:27.540 --> 11:28.750
to searching my notes!

11:30.760 --> 11:34.500
Let's see, four credits... 
A four-credit monster...

11:34.500 --> 11:37.100
I seem to remember from 
Professor Bruno's lecture...

11:37.100 --> 11:41.520
Um, let me see... Maybe it's...

11:39.190 --> 11:41.370
Well, you know...

11:42.420 --> 11:44.080
I'm just talking to myself here,

11:44.080 --> 11:47.890
but there have been reports of a 
Baskerville on the sixth floor.

11:48.230 --> 11:52.280
And a certain book learner 
apparently hasn't defeated one yet.

11:53.940 --> 11:56.820
Thank you so much, Professor Workner!

11:57.410 --> 12:00.760
You dolt! 
Stop clinging to me! It's stifling!

12:00.760 --> 12:02.070
You don't really mind, do you?

12:02.070 --> 12:03.880
Let go, Will!

12:06.490 --> 12:09.410
<i>A Baskerville on the sixth floor...</i>

12:10.230 --> 12:14.420
<i>With this, I'll be rid of that
no-talent who's out of his league.</i>

12:17.880 --> 12:20.960
<b><u>Will Serfort</u>

Race: Rhizanth
Age: 15
Height: 168 cm
Birthday:
24th of Ellsmoon
Likes: Ice candy
Dislikes: Medicinal
morrie herbs
First love: A girl he met when he was little

Deepest Dungeon Floor Reached:  XX  7th
Equipment: Moria silver sword,
battle garb precision crafted by Rosty,
Promise Goggles
Skill: Sword strikes that can fend off even magic

He came from the same orphanage as his
childhood friend, Elfaria. Being talentless, his
inability to use magic has isolated him,
but he is a warrior with a knack for
close-quarters combat.

*Workner has made a redaction on this page</b>

12:30.970 --> 12:35.980
<b>Dungeon, Floor 6</b>

12:32.230 --> 12:33.490
All right!

12:33.490 --> 12:35.980
Tonight, I'm going to get myself four credits!

12:36.280 --> 12:38.980
After all, I've fought a Baskerville before!

12:42.530 --> 12:44.290
It'll be all right.

12:44.290 --> 12:48.950
As long as I'm mindful of its flame breath, 
we won't get burned to a crisp like last time.

12:51.930 --> 12:53.740
So, please, Kiki!

12:54.020 --> 12:55.870
I'm depending on your nose!

12:58.750 --> 13:01.500
We have no need for the
 talentless at our academy.

13:02.100 --> 13:04.130
You think the same, don't you?

13:04.790 --> 13:07.110
Yeah, you're right, Sion.

13:07.110 --> 13:10.480
We'll take care of the monster 
before dealing with that laggard.

13:10.890 --> 13:15.060
That way, he'll be expelled 
for falling short on credits.

13:15.650 --> 13:19.390
But is this really safe, Sion?

13:19.650 --> 13:22.040
Us three coming to floor 6 like this...

13:24.020 --> 13:25.010
Huh?

13:25.650 --> 13:28.400
Don't you know who I am?

13:28.400 --> 13:31.580
S-Sorry! He didn't mean it that way.

13:31.580 --> 13:34.030
Yeah, you're one of the elites, Sion!

13:44.310 --> 13:50.130
<i>In this world, a guy who can't use magic 
shouldn't even speak of the Magia Vander.</i>

13:50.130 --> 13:52.240
<i>It's grating. The very sight 
of him offends me.</i>

13:52.640 --> 13:55.810
<i>He has no right to stay at the academy.</i>

13:57.270 --> 14:00.310
Our target is the Baskerville.

14:00.310 --> 14:02.070
First, we'll cast Search on this area to—

14:25.430 --> 14:26.800
<i>That scream was...</i>

14:27.820 --> 14:31.320
<i>Don't tell me someone 
on this floor is being attacked!</i>

14:32.890 --> 14:36.510
<i>Based on the reverberations, 
they shouldn't be far from here.</i>

14:50.000 --> 14:51.990
<i>An Evil Sentinel?</i>

14:52.610 --> 14:53.860
<i>That's worth ten credits!</i>

14:53.860 --> 14:56.960
<i>A real over-five enemy in the flesh!</i>

15:00.980 --> 15:04.000
<i>The sentinels' habitat should be deeper down.</i>

15:04.310 --> 15:06.240
<i>Did it come up to this floor?</i>

15:06.240 --> 15:07.450
<i>Moreover, that's...</i>

15:07.750 --> 15:08.870
<i>Sion!</i>

15:09.340 --> 15:10.510
S-Stay away!

15:10.980 --> 15:12.270
Stay away!

15:16.970 --> 15:18.760
<i>His magic isn't having any effect.</i>

15:18.760 --> 15:20.770
<i>This monster's on a whole other level!</i>

15:22.800 --> 15:23.740
Blast it!

15:25.030 --> 15:26.660
<i>He doesn't stand a chance.</i>

15:35.640 --> 15:36.930
<i>I have to help him.</i>

15:37.920 --> 15:40.490
<i>No, wait...</i>

15:41.670 --> 15:45.420
<i>Do I actually have any obligation to save him?</i>

15:48.710 --> 15:50.540
<i>After the way he's made fun of me?</i>

15:53.690 --> 15:56.390
<i>He's bullied me to no end, hasn't he?</i>

16:02.220 --> 16:04.230
<i>If I run away, wouldn't it...</i>

16:06.490 --> 16:09.000
I know, you know?

16:23.250 --> 16:25.660
I know, you know?

16:26.170 --> 16:27.800
Will, you're kind...

16:28.460 --> 16:31.020
and braver than anyone.

16:40.420 --> 16:42.290
<i>You're wrong, Elfie.</i>

16:43.070 --> 16:47.080
<i>All I want is to stand beside you.</i>

16:48.530 --> 16:51.610
<i>To be worthy of you.</i>

16:52.100 --> 16:54.430
<i>I'm just a regular pathetic, shameful guy.</i>

17:01.280 --> 17:02.660
<i>That's why, at the very least...</i>

17:10.050 --> 17:12.520
<i>I will become like a lone sword!</i>

17:14.500 --> 17:15.870
Workner!

17:16.860 --> 17:18.620
Professor Edward.

17:18.620 --> 17:20.200
What brings you here at this hour?

17:20.200 --> 17:22.600
Sion and his lot went to
the dungeon without permission.

17:22.600 --> 17:24.240
What did you say?!

17:24.240 --> 17:26.100
That blasted whelp of a noble...

17:26.450 --> 17:30.230
The dungeon is vast. Use your 
familiar to find their whereabouts.

17:30.720 --> 17:32.730
What floor were they headed to?

17:32.730 --> 17:33.730
Floor 6.

17:38.540 --> 17:40.940
In that case, there's no need for this.

17:41.660 --> 17:42.520
What?

17:44.790 --> 17:46.740
Will is there.

18:37.960 --> 18:40.050
<i>What's this?</i>

18:41.010 --> 18:44.220
<i>Is that really the same Will?</i>

18:52.730 --> 18:54.600
I-Impossible!

18:55.530 --> 18:57.730
Will is a true outlier.

18:58.220 --> 18:59.670
What do you mean?

19:03.770 --> 19:05.870
Superhuman strength
a mage would never possess.

19:09.460 --> 19:11.720
A physique as robust as a dwarf's.

19:17.410 --> 19:21.720
And the observational skills to grasp an
 enemy's strategies after seeing them just once.

19:25.760 --> 19:27.350
<i>I've already...</i>

19:28.890 --> 19:29.990
<i>seen that!</i>

19:36.930 --> 19:39.820
It's true that Will can't use 
the slightest bit of magic.

19:46.200 --> 19:47.280
However...

19:48.200 --> 19:50.160
In this world full of magic,

19:50.640 --> 19:52.160
he's the one and only warrior!

20:17.910 --> 20:18.940
A slash of his sword...

20:21.740 --> 20:23.540
surpasses even lightning!

20:46.490 --> 20:48.720
You're not hurt, are you?

20:54.400 --> 20:55.850
You must be joking!

20:55.850 --> 20:57.940
I won't stand for this!

20:58.390 --> 21:02.690
Someone who can't even use magic
is able to surpass it?!

21:03.450 --> 21:04.860
Professor Edward!

21:26.530 --> 21:30.220
Will Serfort is hereby awarded ten credits.

21:32.870 --> 21:34.970
All right!

21:35.980 --> 21:40.350
<i>This is the story of a boy 
who would turn the world on its head.</i>

21:45.530 --> 21:48.540
<i>A tale of the joining of
 wand and sword, Wistoria.</i>

23:37.570 --> 23:39.850
Next time on <i>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</i>,

23:40.230 --> 23:42.640
episode 2, "As Though Undaunted."

23:41.100 --> 23:45.980
Episode 2
As Though Undaunted
